text tpicg6 "The diff is empty."
note gpimp: the loaded item is imported (1) or signed (0); gpist: its status (0 open, 1 closed, 2
note merged); gpider: its state is derived (code-only); gpicode: its code file (0 none, 1 mbox, 2
note head.bundle; its size in gpmby); gpihb: it has a base (gpbase); gpnum: its GitHub number; gpbd:
note the bundle diff (pabdiff's answer; 9 not asked); gpsc: the items a list page shows by state (list
note head); gptr: why the comments of forge/patch/1 are not the whole thread (pajcoms: 0 they are, 1 a
note malformed record, 2 the thread file is larger than gpth, 3 the document budget PAJMX)
global gpimp ulong 1
global gpist ulong 1
global gpider ulong 1
global gpicode ulong 1
global gpihb ulong 1
global gpnum ulong 1
global gpbd ulong 1
global gpsc ulong 3
global gptr ulong 1
note gpr: offsets and lengths of the parsers (thread record, gh line, source.json value, reach line)
global gpr ulong 16
note gpsrc: source.json (its first 4096 bytes); gpgh: the gh file (its first 2048 bytes); gpth: the
note thread (as much as fxo reads; gpthc 1 when the file is larger)
global gpsrc uchar 4096
global gpsrcl ulong 1
global gpgh uchar 2048
global gpghl ulong 1
global gpth uchar 16777216
global gpthl ulong 1
global gpthc ulong 1
note PAPGMX: the most an imported page's description and thread take of fob (8 MiB), so the
note provenance box and a 400000-byte diff (6 bytes each at most, escaped) still fit after them
const PAPGMX ulong 5000000
note PAJMX: the most forge/patch/1 takes of fob (8388608 bytes) up to the end of its comments. The
note 65536 bytes left hold the rest of the document: at most 24578 bytes of "created" (a source.json
note value of up to 4096 bytes, 6 bytes each escaped), four links of under 250 bytes and the fixed keys
const PAJMX ulong 8323072
